id: liquid-sixth-effect
name: 6th effect of Liquid State
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/round
surge: true
surgeKind: healing
fromTrait: liquid
fromEffect: 6
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The Liquid Special State's sixth effect, as a Maneuver: a Healing Surge for 1 Action,
  once a Combat Round, for as long as you are Liquid.
text: >
  (6)-[1/Round]: As a Standard Action with an Action Cost of 1 Action, you may use a
  Healing Surge.

---

# The first Maneuver in this system that is somebody else's effect.
#
# Some effects hand you a Maneuver rather than doing something themselves, and the Liquid
# Special State's sixth is one: "as a Standard Action with an Action Cost of 1 Action, you
# may use a Healing Surge". Everything the system needs to know about that is what it
# knows about any Maneuver - a type, an Action Cost, a limit, and what using it does - so
# it is one, rather than a shape invented to hold it.
#
# --- Why it is a Maneuver Item like the rest ----------------------------------------------
#
# Because a player will change it. The name here is a description rather than a name - the
# rulebook gives this effect none - and somebody whose character liquefies every fight will
# want to call it what they call it. An Item is what remembers that.
#
# So every character owns this from the day they are made, exactly like the Basic Attack,
# and `fromTrait` is what keeps it out of their list until they are actually Liquid. The
# alternative - creating it when the State is entered and deleting it when the State ends -
# would take their name with it every time they solidified.
#
# --- What it names -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `fromTrait: liquid` is the Trait it belongs to and `fromEffect: 6` is which of that
# Trait's numbered effects it is. Both are read: the first decides when the row appears and
# the second is what the name is built from, so a reader can find the sentence this came
# from.
#
# `surgeKind: healing` is the other half of the rule. The Surge Maneuver offers both and
# asks which; this one names Healing, and asking would be asking a question the entry has
# already answered.
#
# --- What is not here -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Anything about being Liquid. What the State is worth is in the State's file, and this is
# one line out of it - the line that happens to be a Maneuver.
